{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I commanded you.</b> He speaks with the tribes of Reuben and Gad. Because they were included in all Israel, he said \"you\" and not \"them.\" The reverse of this is \"And Moses commanded the Levites, saying: Take this book of the Torah\" (Deuteronomy 31:24–26), and \"For I know your rebellion\" (Deuteronomy 31:27) — he is not speaking to the Levites but to all Israel, and because the Levites were included, he spoke to them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:07.675746624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}